{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"shimmery-customary-dorking","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Suspected defect\nA source-path audit at code revision d49466b5e960 suggests that one completion operation may combine code evidence read from the immutable tree selected by `--ref` with prefetch, deterministic checks, or later signing inputs rooted at the live checkout. This is a hypothesis from control-flow inspection, not a demonstrated failure. It MUST be verified experimentally before any production change.\n\nThe public contract is that checks which judge the implementation are based on the code revision supplied by `--ref`. Comparisons against live state can be valid for drift detection, ancestry, optimistic concurrency, or publication safety, but live checkout content must not become verdict evidence for a `--ref`-targeted run.\n\n## Mandatory reproduction before remediation\n1. Build a disposable Git fixture with revisions A and B whose source, referencing commit evidence, and a prefetched file deliberately disagree. Keep the live checkout at B and invoke the real completion path with `--ref A`.\n2. Instrument or spy on every code-root/ref input used by context assembly, completion prefetch, deterministic commit/file checks, verifier tools, drift checks, and completion-signature material. Record the resolved OID and classify each read as verdict evidence, ticket-state evidence, or an intentional live-state comparison.\n3. Prove whether all verdict-bearing code reads resolve to A. If they do, record the falsification and close this bug without a speculative refactor. If any verdict-bearing read resolves to B, preserve the failing experiment as the regression test before changing code.\n\n## Remediation constraints if reproduced\n- Thread one explicit pinned-code handle/OID through every verdict-bearing path; do not let a generic `repo_root` silently select live code.\n- Keep intentional live comparisons explicit and one-way: they may reject/retry stale work, but may not contribute evidence that makes a criterion pass or fail.\n- Bind `verified_at_sha` and the completion signature to the same A selected by `--ref`.\n- Cover a moving branch name as well as a concrete SHA, resolving the name once at operation start.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A deterministic divergent-A/B experiment proves or falsifies the suspected mixed-root behavior through the real completion orchestration path.\n- [ ] The evidence records the resolved OID and purpose of every code read used by prefetch, deterministic checks, agent file tools, drift comparison, and signing.\n- [ ] If reproduced, a regression test fails before the fix when live=B and `--ref=A`, then passes only when every verdict-bearing check uses A.\n- [ ] Intentional live-state comparisons are named and tested to fail closed or retry without becoming verdict evidence.\n- [ ] The emitted `verified_at_sha` and signed completion manifest equal A.\n- [ ] If the experiment falsifies the hypothesis, no production behavior is changed and the ticket closes with the falsifying evidence.","id":"831f-326d-be85-437a","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["completion-verifier","pinned-ref","correctness","experiment-first"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"--ref-targeted completion may mix pinned code with live-checkout inputs"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787678967773233001,"uuid":"c86e031a-763d-42e5-8338-be3ab983aa71"}